Fri Oct  2 05:45:42 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.9.1:
  * Expose cooperative cancellation on TokenParser:
    enable_cancellation() is idempotent and cancellation_handle()
    returns the parser's existing cancellation state once
    enabled. Cancellation stays opt-in and parser behaviour is
    unchanged when it is not enabled
- Re-generate registry.tar.zst for 1.9.1 via the cargo_vendor
  service: pyo3 0.29.2 -> 0.29.3 and lazy_static 1.5.0 ->
  1.5.1, all permissive. License is unchanged, but correct the
  Legal-Review-Notice MIT count, which understated it: 22 of
  the 111 linked crates grant MIT, not 21

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Sep 30 08:19:32 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.9.0:
  * Add opt-in cooperative cancellation for abandoned matcher
    computations: disabled by default, enabled via Rust
    Matcher::into_cancellable() or the new C cancellation-handle API;
    cancelled matchers stop with StopReason::Cancelled and their
    forced-output methods return empty results
  * Compile homogeneous bounded JSON array tails compactly
    (logarithmic repetition) instead of one grammar entry per item,
    avoiding compact-grammar symbol overflow for large maxItems
  * Parse compact Lark tilde repeat ranges such as HI~0..2
  * Report empty integer intervals in JSON schemas as
    UnsatisfiableSchemaError instead of a regex-generation error
  * Update derivre to 0.3.13: patterns with redundant nested anchors,
    e.g. ^(^foo$)$|^$, now compile
- Re-generate registry.tar.zst for 1.9.0 via the cargo_vendor service:
  17 linked crates bumped past upstream's lock, all permissive;
  pyo3 0.29.2; License unchanged, Legal-Review-Notice re-derived from
  the new registry with the unlinked crate attribution corrected

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Aug 11 05:34:17 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.8.0:
  * Allow general Unicode escapes in JSON strings and object keys
  * Support \xHH escapes in Lark string literals
  * Add single-match skip lexemes
  * Preserve the exclusiveMinimum/exclusiveMaximum names in JSON
    Schema errors instead of reporting them as minimum/maximum
  * Accept negative numbers in multipleOf, which previously rejected
    every negative value, including valid negative multiples
  * Treat max_tokens=0 as an empty string instead of compiling a
    token-limited lexeme that never terminates at runtime
  * Harden the C FFI layer: catch_unwind guards on the extern "C"
    entry points, null tolerance in all llg_free_* functions, a
    fixed buffer-sizing bug and a new C++ FFI test suite
  * Add CI support for Windows ARM64 Python wheels
  * Update pyo3 to 0.29.0
- Re-generate registry.tar.zst for 1.8.0 via the cargo_vendor service
- Narrow License to Apache-2.0 AND MIT AND MIT-0 AND Unicode-3.0:
  the tag is now derived from the 111 crates maturin actually
  compiles into the extension module rather than from the whole
  workspace lockfile. The previously declared BSD-3-Clause,
  CDLA-Permissive-2.0, ISC and MPL-2.0 come solely from the HTTP and
  TLS stack of the toktrie_hf_downloader workspace member and from a
  dev-dependency of the parser crate, neither of which is built
  here; the derivation is recorded as a Legal-Review-Notice in the
  spec file
- Declare the rust-version floor the workspace manifest sets by
  adding BuildRequires on rust >= 1.87

